modStarterQuestGearUp:
{#--color-brown:Attacking creatures will use items in your inventory when equipped to your main hand. Let's equip an item now.}

1. Open your equipment {(HELP/INTERFACE):dialog} with {BINDINGS:DialogEquipment} or click the equipment icon at the top of the screen.

2. Equip a tool or weapon by dragging it from your inventory to the equipment slot of your choice.

Alternatively, you can {BINDINGS:GameItemEquipToggle} to toggle it equipped or not.

{(HELP/HELD_ITEMS):Learn more about Held Items}

modStarterQuestActionSlots:
{#--color-brown:When hovering over a tile, actions can be used via the action menu (performed with {BINDINGS:GameActions}) or the item action menu (performed with {BINDINGS:GameActionsItems}). Performing actions in this way can be tedious.}

Instead, you can use actions in your action bar so they can be performed with a single hotkey.

By default, if you have not played before, you will already have some actions setup in your action bar including "Pick Up All Items", performed with {BINDINGS:GameActionBarUseSlot0}, or "Chop", performed with {BINDINGS:GameActionBarUseSlot1}. 

To add an additional action to an action slot, simply hover over a free action slot, for example, slot #6, and use {BINDINGS:GameActionBarConfigure}. Choose "Harvest" from the action menu that comes up and click "Done".

Now you can use the binding that is shown under the action slot.

{#--color-brown:Using actions in this way will always pick the "best" item for the action from your inventory.}

modStarterQuestItemActionSlots:
{#--color-brown:All items have a list of actions that can be performed with them at any time.}

{BINDINGS:GameItemMenu} to open an item's action menu.

{#--color-brown:Using actions in this way can be cumbersome. You can also use the action bar for items!}

- Drag and drop an item into an action slot.

- OR use one of the "Assign Action" bindings. While hovering over an item, use {BINDINGS:GameActionBarAssignSlot6}, {BINDINGS:GameActionBarAssignSlot7}, or {BINDINGS:GameActionBarAssignSlot8} for example to use slot 7/8/9.

{#--color-brown:This is a sequence bind, meaning you have to press one key, then the other instead of all at the same time.}

modStarterQuestRepairingItemsDurability:
{#--color-brown:Items can break over time, especially if they are used frequently as you've most likely noticed. Their durability is consumed when used in an action, damaged in combat (if they are equipment), or used in crafts. Most items can be repaired while some others might need more advanced techniques in order to increase their durability. Let's create a "{/Granite Hammer/}" which will enable the repair action to show up in each item's action menu if available.}

To create the hammer, we will need the following:

1. "{/Wooden Pole/}" - You created some of these earlier through dismantling.
2. "{/String/}" - Can be crafted with 2 cordage items, like stripped bark, plant roots, or sinew.
3. "{/Granite/}" - We also collected some of these earlier.

{#--color-brown:After crafting the hammer, to repair an item, you can use the "{/Repair/}" action from the item's menu that you want to repair. You can also use the repair action from the hammer's menu, but this will repair items in front of the player instead (items on the ground or doodads). This will consume durability from the tool used to repair it and in this case, the granite hammer.}

